l":"https://api.github.com/repos/babel/babel/labels/i:%20question","name":"i: question","color":"e99695","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2018-09-16T01:54:06Z","updated_at":"2025-01-22T20:05:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"In babel 7, there is a new `loadPartialConfig` API that resolves a babel config for a file. Along with resolving the config files, it also does some config normalization, and even loads and executes plugin and preset modules.

While useful, this function does too much for some use cases. For example, in Parcel, we support automatically installing plugins and presets for you when you add them to your babelrc, and additionally do some merging of configs with internally generated ones. We also need to support backward compatibility with babel 6, which doesn't support the normalized config items that babel 7 returns.

I would like to introduce an even more granular API to babel that would allow tools like Parcel to use more pieces of babel's infrastructure rather than reimplementing it. The pieces are as follows.

1. Add a new function `resolveConfig` (naming TBD), which works like `loadPartialConfig` but does fewer things.
    - Finds and reads config files, following all rules e.g. `extends`, `include`, `exclude`, `.babelignore`, `babel.config.js`, etc. Merges configs as necessary. Returns `null` if the file would be ignored.
    - Returns non-normalized plugins and presets (i.e. does not convert them to `ConfigItem`). They should be returned exactly as they were specified in the config files.
    - Does not resolve or load any plugins or presets, just returns the names as they were specified in the config file. This will allow tools like Parcel to use the names to e.g. auto install plugins with a package manager.
    - Returns a list of all files that it read in order to load the config, including any `extends` files, and `.babelrc` files that did not match due to `include`/`exclude` rules. These need to be exposed so bundlers can watch the files for changes.
2. Add a new function `normalizePluginName` (naming TBD) to convert a plugin/preset name to a fully resolved name, e.g. `@babel/env` to `@babel/preset-env`. External tools need to have access to this utility so they can perform their own resolution, e.g. installing packages automatically.
4. Expose `makeAPI` function so that other tools can call plugin/preset functions themselves. Parcel does this to do a diff between plugins returned by `babel-preset-env` to only include the plugins necessary to compile a module to the app's target.
5. Make `loadPartialConfig` and `loadOptions` support passing whatever `resolveConfig` returns, so that the full config can be loaded including presets and plugins. This should already work if `resolveConfig` does not touch the config file that came from disk.

With these options available, we would need to do a lot less reimplementing of babel's internals in Parcel. Babel 7's config resolution is pretty complicated, so I would really like to avoid that if possible. If this proposal is accepted, I am happy to assist with the implementation in babel.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/babel/babel/issues/8715/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/babel/babel/issues/8715/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/babel/babel/issues/15679","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/babel/babel","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/babel/babel/issues/15679/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/babel/babel/issues/15679/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/babel/babel/issues/15679/events","html_url":"https://github.com/babel/babel/issues/15679","id":1738322292,"node_id":"I_kwDOAXbCs85nnLF0","number":15679,"title":"[Bug]: Breaking change in a minor version bump","user":{"login":"schneems","id":59744,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59744?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems","html_url":"https://github.com/schneems","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/schneems/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https: